                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "77b7c815-131d-3dc9-9fb6-3fb40eedd283",
                        "entry_id": "a42af7a0-fdf4-3f07-9ee7-b53943aa3e97",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To noisily try to convince others."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5320efd2-2516-45d6-861e-131b3faa8807",
                                "sense_id": "77b7c815-131d-3dc9-9fb6-3fb40eedd283",
                                "text": "\"The crisis of Olympia's destiny will come and pass,\" Stevens fretted, \"and the die be cast against her while her people are wraggling over... 'bonds.'\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "171238e5-879f-4f7b-9e57-a42430d11515",
                                "sense_id": "77b7c815-131d-3dc9-9fb6-3fb40eedd283",
                                "text": "'The business of water transportation knows no haggling and wraggling', said the boatman blatantly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5eb9c550-a515-4c42-b6c9-f7f19ecfcb56",
                                "sense_id": "77b7c815-131d-3dc9-9fb6-3fb40eedd283",
                                "text": "Amid the wildest hubbub produced by the shouting, wraggling, jabbering of the owners of the beasts, each man praising the qualities of his own animal as he dragged it to the front, the naval party managed to mount;"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b8914001-cd83-3180-bdfc-b9df07aa3146",
                        "entry_id": "a42af7a0-fdf4-3f07-9ee7-b53943aa3e97",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To pester."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "048cf33e-ab4f-485a-887a-0fa3c570b5e9",
                                "sense_id": "b8914001-cd83-3180-bdfc-b9df07aa3146",
                                "text": "They represent the first record of Fur Seals in this area and it is intented that meteorological and hydrological conditions in the Tasman Sea during austral winter have wraggled to the north young Fur Seals from probably south-australian populations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "926b42f8-aa39-4996-bacd-6fa3754171a7",
                                "sense_id": "b8914001-cd83-3180-bdfc-b9df07aa3146",
                                "text": "Remember you're tired from wraggling with those nasty customers all day, or pounding out dull, business letters."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1f02a08-3d01-4da3-81bc-62e0d6277048",
                                "sense_id": "b8914001-cd83-3180-bdfc-b9df07aa3146",
                                "text": "On the other hand, if he failed to make the pitiable noises Baron Skulkrak seemed to relish, then His Horribleness might surely apply further unpleasant techniques to wraggle that out of his victims."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
